# Dogfood — our nexus deploy manifest

This is the **deploy root's `index.work`** — the deploy-as-index-tree manifest (see
`nexus/docs/deploy-as-index-tree.md`). The deploy block here configures this whole tree: it's read by
`Nexus.Config` at boot (`$WB_DATA/index.work`), and it is the **only** place a `deploy` block takes
effect — one per index, no sidecar, no magic filename. This index is the composition root + manifest,
**not** a served surface (mount discovery skips it); the surfaces are the subfolders
([[lander]], [[cloud]], [[docs]], …).

This is the **our-cloud side of THE LINE**: the runtime ships neutral, and *our* values live here, as
config — never env vars, never constants in `lib/`. Dogfooding: we run our own nexus the exact way we
ask everyone else to — a `.work` config declaration in the deploy index, read at boot. Secrets are NOT
here — those come through `Nexus.Secrets` from the encrypted control-plane store.

deploy do
  # Our capacity tiers — the numbers the dashboard + the upsell read. `id | Name | ram_mb storage_gb price_usd domains(yes|no)`.
  # No free tier: a nexus is an always-on Fly machine, so the floor is the smallest real machine ($20).
  # Grounded in DeployKit/Fly cost (always-on shared-CPU machine + volume) at ~2.2–2.4x. Mirrored by
  # the lander's cloud-tiers section. (Enterprise is custom — not a fixed row.)
  tiers="
    solo   | Solo   | 512 10 12 no
    studio | Studio | 2048 75 32 yes
    team   | Team   | 4096 200 89 yes
    scale  | Scale  | 8192 500 229 yes
  "

  # Our nexus's display emoji + its WORKSPACES — curated folders of work, NOT every mount. Each line:
  # `folder | Name | emoji`. The dashboard reads these; the UI emoji picker overrides an icon per-org.
  nexus-emoji="🐕"
  # Three workspaces; surfaces nest under them (cloud/overview, lander/blog, …). The workspace id IS its
  # on-disk folder; an app's workspace = its path's first segment. (login stays top-level — auth URL.)
  workspaces="
    cloud  | Cloud  | ☁️
    lander | Lander | 🪧
    docs   | Docs   | 📖
  "

  reserved-hosts="workbooks.sh"                          # our domain of record — tenants can't bind under it
  runtime-image="ghcr.io/workbooks-sh/runtime:latest"   # the image we provision per-tenant

  # Cloudflare-for-SaaS custom hostnames — the cheap, edge-TLS path for customer domains. When set, a
  # custom-domain bind issues a CF per-hostname cert (first 100 free) instead of a per-app Fly cert; the
  # owner points one CNAME at the fallback origin below. The CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN is a SECRET (injected),
  # never config. Empty ⇒ Nexus.ControlPlane.Domain stays on the Fly-cert path.
  cf-saas-zone="6db3a52031b1b90111e8d77b6fbaed36"        # workbooks.sh zone id
  cf-custom-hostname-origin="customers.workbooks.sh"     # CNAME target customers point their domain at

  search="brave"                                         # cloud web-search: keyed Brave (reliable from datacenter IPs)
  compile-cache="on"
end
